{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"bc1d50830d492c351c83758b97c58bacc8a8f9961f85515f07567f46a367acfe","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar-mcp server HTTP transport + auth framework","key_entities":["src/rebar/mcp_server.py","FastMCP","mcp.server.auth.provider.TokenVerifier","verify_token","AccessToken.resource","AuthSettings","TransportSecuritySettings","streamable_http_app()","auth_resource_server_url","mcp.auth_strategies","REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED_HTTP","REBAR_MCP_READONLY","McpConfig","MCP_ENV_VARS","server.json","scripts/check_server_manifest.py","docs/mcp-auth.md","docs/mcp-reference.md","docs/env-vars.md","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py","mcp>=1.28.1,<2","pyjwt[crypto]","RFC 8707","RFC 7662"],"problem_keywords":["mcp authentication","oauth 2.1 resource server","bearer token validation","streamable-http transport","rfc 9728 protected resource metadata","token audience validation","fail-closed startup","dns-rebinding protection","provider-agnostic auth","jwks/jwt verifier","introspection verifier","trusted-proxy passthrough","static bearer token","confused-deputy prevention"],"propositions":["rebar-mcp is stdio-only with no HTTP transport and no authentication, so a shared/hosted rebar store cannot be reached by a remote MCP client without exposing it unauthenticated.","This epic adds an optional Streamable-HTTP transport where rebar acts as an OAuth 2.1 Resource Server that validates inbound bearer tokens and advertises RFC 9728 Protected Resource Metadata, delegating identity to a deploying org's IdP.","A composite TokenVerifier is the single audience/fail-closed choke point that re-validates every token's resource equals the single configured auth_resource_server_url, since the SDK never inspects token audience.","Five selectable verifier modes ship: static bearer, JWKS/JWT, RFC 7662 introspection, trusted-proxy passthrough, and pluggable custom, each populating AccessToken.resource.","With auth enabled an unauthenticated request receives 401 plus a WWW-Authenticate header carrying the RFC 9728 resource_metadata URL; misconfiguration and auth-downgrade paths refuse to start (fail-closed).","Changes are purely additive: stdio remains the default transport, auth is off by default, and rollback is config-level by leaving new flat mcp.* keys unset."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785203276818430389,"uuid":"4cee5932-c4a3-457a-9740-55f1d45f488d"}